<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riksdag of the Estates</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as four estates</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riksdag">Riksdag</a> of the Estates was the form of the Swedish parliament in which representatives sat in four separate estates: the nobility, the clergy, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> and the peasantry. Its inclusion of a peasant estate was unusual among European assemblies of the time. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> describe the four estates as part of the governing framework through which the crown mobilised resources for its wars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riksdag-of-the-estates.jpg" alt="Riksdag of the Estates" width="320" height="306" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_coat_of_arms_of_Sweden_(without_mantle).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
